From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Nov 2026 07:20:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: send a gen2 decoder's input parameters only
 before the firmware parses the stream

When a video loops or seeks, Chromium drains the decoder and restarts
both queues. At each STREAMON of the input queue iris sent the decoder's
input parameters again: its bitstream resolution aligned to 16
(1920x1088) and its minimum output count (4). The firmware had parsed
1920x1080 and 11, so after the seek it compared and reported a settings
change (HFI_CMD_SETTINGS_CHANGE) but never returned the last buffer of
the old sequence. Chromium waits for that LAST buffer before it
reconfigures, so the video stopped after its first pass, at 94 of 300
frames, and after two such stalls Chromium decoded every video in
software.

msm_vidc sends these parameters only with its first subscription to
port settings changes. Do the same: once the input subscription is set,
skip them.

Tested on a KONKR Pocket FIT Elite (SM8750, vpu35_p4.mbn) in the Steam
client: startup_machine.webm (1080p VP9) loops at 299 of 300 frames in
10 s with no settings change after the first, and Steam's 1920x1200
startup movies loop at 600 of 600.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
index 388a36f..9eb9d41 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
@@ -668,6 +668,7 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_set_super_block(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 static int iris_hfi_gen2_session_set_config_params(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 {
 	const struct iris_firmware_data *fdata = inst->core->iris_firmware_data;
+	struct iris_inst_hfi_gen2 *inst_hfi_gen2 = to_iris_inst_hfi_gen2(inst);
 	u32 config_params_size = 0, i, j;
 	const u32 *config_params = NULL;
 	int ret;
@@ -693,6 +694,15 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_session_set_config_params(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 p
 		{HFI_PROP_AV1_SUPER_BLOCK_ENABLED,    iris_hfi_gen2_set_super_block            },
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The decoder's input parameters go to the firmware once, before it has parsed the
+	 * stream, as msm_vidc does. Sent again after a seek, our aligned guesses differ from
+	 * what it parsed, and it reports a settings change that never completes.
+	 */
+	if (inst->domain == DECODER && V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane) &&
+	    inst_hfi_gen2->ipsc_properties_set)
+		return 0;
+
 	if (inst->domain == DECODER) {
 		if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane)) {
 			if (inst->codec == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264) {
-- 
